import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
public class Solution {
    public static int largestPrimeFactor(int n) {

        // Step 1: Remove all factors of 2
        int maxFactor = -1;
        while(n % 2 == 0){
            maxFactor = 2;
            n /= 2;
        }

        // Step 2: Check odd numbers from 3 up to sqrt(n)
         for(int i = 3; i * i <= n;i++){
            while(n % i == 0){
                maxFactor = i;
                n /= i;
            }
        }
        // Step 3: If n is still > 2, then n is prime
            if(n > 2){
            maxFactor = n;
        }
        return maxFactor;
    }
}


You are given a positive integer ‘n’. Your task is to find the largest prime factor of this given positive integer.
Note :
If there is no prime factor of a given integer, then print -1.

T.C => O(N + O(N logN))
S.C => O(1)
